title: Rule-of-Law Repair
subtitle: Begin with a complete constitutional reset of the courts; case-by-case triage is a fallback, not a first rung.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_major_reform_card
frequency: 130
view-if: month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_courts_reform_timer <= 0 and courts_reform_settled = 0 and courts_on_slate = 1 and reform_pressure_pending = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.month_actions += 1;
Q.poland_courts_reform_timer = 3;
Q.courts_reform_next_stage = Number(Q.courts_reform_proposal_stage) || 4;
const thresholds = [0, 26, 42, 62, 86];
Q.courts_reform_threshold = thresholds[Q.courts_reform_next_stage];
const ministryBonus =
    (Q.justice_minister_party == "Lewica" ? 14 : 0) +
    (Q.digital_minister_party == "Lewica" ? 3 : 0);
const koCabinet = Q.government_party == "ko" || Q.ministry_ko_in_cabinet;
const pslCabinet = Q.government_party == "psl" || Q.ministry_psl_in_cabinet;
const p2050Cabinet =
    Q.government_party == "p2050" || Q.ministry_p2050_in_cabinet;
const thirdWayCabinet = pslCabinet || p2050Cabinet;
let partnerBonus = 0;
if (Q.government_party == "pis") {
    // A PiS-led cabinet does not repair the courts it built.
    partnerBonus = -40 + Number(Q.courts_pis_commitment) * 5;
} else {
    partnerBonus =
        (koCabinet
            ? Number(Q.ko_relation) * 0.12 +
                Number(Q.courts_ko_commitment) * 8 + 6
            : 0) +
        (thirdWayCabinet
            ? Number(Q.courts_third_way_commitment) * 5 +
                (p2050Cabinet
                    ? Number(Q.p2050_state_capacity_share) * 0.06
                    : 0)
            : 0);
}
const palaceBonus =
    Number(Q.president_relation) * 0.07 +
    (Q.courts_palace_president == Q.president_name
        ? Number(Q.courts_palace_commitment) * 6
        : 0);
const publicBonus =
    (Number(Q.rule_of_law_support) - 45) * 0.35 +
    Number(Q.judicial_repair_mandate) * 0.12 +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_poll) - 5) * 0.45 -
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.rule_of_law_backlash) - 50) * 0.14;
Q.courts_reform_power = Math.round(Math.max(
    0,
    Math.min(
        140,
        Number(Q.courts_reform_progress) * 0.62 +
        partnerBonus + palaceBonus + publicBonus + ministryBonus +
        Number(Q.constitutional_restraint) * 0.4
    )
));
Q.reform_ceiling_issue = "courts";
Q.reform_ceiling_target = Q.courts_reform_next_stage;
!}
call: poland_reform_ceiling
card-image: img/poland/cards/group-institutional.webp

= The courts as a whole-game project

**Campaign goal:** [? if courts_reform_defined: [+ courts_reform_goal_label
+].?][? if not courts_reform_defined: Not yet defined.?]
[? if courts_reform_defined: **Bill currently on the table:** [+
courts_reform_next_label +].
**Passage power:** **[+ courts_reform_power +]**; tabling this bill needs **[+
courts_reform_threshold +]**.
**Settlement ceiling:** [+ reform_ceiling_tier_label +] — [+
reform_ceiling_reachable_label +].
[? if reform_ceiling_blocker_kind != "none": Binding veto player: **[+
reform_ceiling_blocker_name +]** — scores the bill [+
reform_ceiling_blocker_score +] against the [+ reform_ceiling_need +] a tier-[+
reform_ceiling_target_resolved +] settlement needs.?]
[+ reform_ceiling_breakdown +].?][? if not courts_reform_defined: The first
project action must define the ambitious bill before preparation or bargaining
can begin.?]

KO wants this more than we do, which makes it the cheapest reform to pass and
the easiest to pass badly. A reset carried out by resolution rather than statute
repairs the personnel and leaves the precedent that a majority may reorganise
the courts.

[? if legal_dualism > 40: Legal dualism is already deep. Two lines of
authority issue conflicting rulings, and the longer that lasts the more a fast,
lawless repair looks reasonable to our own side.?]

[? if courts_reform_defined and courts_reform_next_stage = 4: A complete
constitutional reset needs a President who will sign it. That is the whole
constraint on this field: no relationship substitutes for a signature on a
Tribunal bill.?]

- @define_goal
- @draft
- @coalition_round
- @cash_relation
- @ministry
- @palace
- @advance

@define_goal
title: Define the goal as a complete lawful reset of the courts
subtitle: KRS, neo-judge status and the Constitutional Tribunal enter as one statutory demand.
view-if: courts_reform_defined = 0
on-arrival: courts_reform_defined = 1; courts_on_slate = 1; courts_reform_goal_stage = 4; courts_reform_proposal_stage = 4; courts_reform_next_stage = 4; courts_reform_progress += 12; constitutional_restraint += 2; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_salience += 3; news_headline = "Lewica defines a lawful constitutional reset as its judicial bill"

Committing to a statutory route now is what makes it possible to refuse the
resolution route later, when the coalition is impatient and the courts are still
broken.

- #poland_card_finish

@draft
title: Keep the constitutionalists and judges drafting
subtitle: Free. Preparation +10.
view-if: courts_reform_defined = 1
on-arrival: courts_reform_progress += 10; judicial_legitimacy += 1; news_headline = "Lewica keeps its lawful judicial-reset statute ready for the next opening"

Constitutional lawyers, sitting judges and the neo-judges' own cases produce a
transition that survives a Tribunal challenge rather than provoking one.

- #poland_card_finish

@coalition_round
title: Put the judicial file on a partner's table
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Choose KO, [+ third_way_display_name +] or PiS and record one commitment.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: A serious negotiating round needs one resource.
view-if: courts_reform_defined = 1
new-page: true

- @round_ko
- @round_third_way
- @round_pis

@round_ko
title: Ask KO to record a statutory-route commitment
on-arrival: resources -= 1; courts_reform_progress += 8; courts_ko_commitment += 1; ko_relation += 4; constitutional_restraint += 1; news_headline = "KO records a statutory route for judicial repair"

KO records that the repair goes through statute rather than ministerial decree.
It is slower than the justice ministry wanted, and it survives the first
constitutional challenge, which the shortcut would not have.

- #poland_card_finish

@round_third_way
title: Make [+ third_way_display_name +] name the transition it would back
view-if: p2050_emerged = 1 or third_way_active = 1
on-arrival: {! Q.resources -= 1; Q.courts_reform_progress += 8; Q.courts_third_way_commitment += 1; Q.psl_relation += 3; Q.p2050_relation += 4; Q.news_headline = Q.third_way_display_name + " records a judicial-transition commitment"; !}

[+ third_way_display_name +] commits to a transition rule for the judges
appointed under the old council. Naming what actually happens to those people
is the part every other party has spent four years avoiding.

- #poland_card_finish

@round_pis
title: Open a neo-judge status channel with PiS
choose-if: (left_in_government = 1 and government_party = "pis") or pis_relation >= 30 or national_crisis_pressure >= 30
unavailable-subtitle: PiS will not discuss the status of its own appointments without coalition ties or acute pressure.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; courts_reform_progress += 5; courts_pis_commitment += 1; pis_relation += 2; news_headline = "PiS opens a narrow channel on neo-judge status"

PiS will discuss the standing of its own appointees as a status question and
never as a legitimacy question. The channel is narrow, and it is the only one
that reaches the people currently sitting on the benches.

- #poland_card_finish

@cash_relation
title: Cash in a party relationship instead of spending a resource
subtitle: Choose a 55+ relationship; it falls by 10 and becomes one recorded commitment.
choose-if: ko_relation >= 55 or pis_relation >= 55 or ((p2050_emerged = 1 or third_way_active = 1) and (psl_relation >= 55 or p2050_relation >= 55))
unavailable-subtitle: No potential governing partner trusts us enough yet.
view-if: courts_reform_defined = 1
new-page: true

- @cash_ko
- @cash_third_way
- @cash_pis

@cash_ko
title: Spend KO goodwill on the lawful judicial route
choose-if: ko_relation >= 55
on-arrival: ko_relation -= 10; courts_ko_commitment += 1; courts_reform_progress += 10; news_headline = "Lewica converts KO goodwill into a lawful judicial route"

The trust buys the lawful route instead of the fast one. Irregular appointments
still have to be unwound case by case, and there is now a majority willing to
write the rule that does it.

- #poland_card_finish

@cash_third_way
title: Spend [+ third_way_display_name +] goodwill on judicial transition
view-if: p2050_emerged = 1 or third_way_active = 1
choose-if: psl_relation >= 55 or p2050_relation >= 55
on-arrival: {!
if (Number(Q.psl_relation) >= Number(Q.p2050_relation)) {
    Q.psl_relation -= 10;
} else {
    Q.p2050_relation -= 10;
}
Q.courts_third_way_commitment += 1;
Q.courts_reform_progress += 10;
Q.news_headline = "Lewica converts " + Q.third_way_display_name + " goodwill into judicial transition";
!}

[+ third_way_display_name +] supplies the transitional clauses that turn a
principle into an administrable statute. The relationship pays for drafting
work nobody else volunteered to do.

- #poland_card_finish

@cash_pis
title: Spend PiS goodwill on neo-judge transition rules
choose-if: pis_relation >= 55
on-arrival: pis_relation -= 10; courts_pis_commitment += 1; courts_reform_progress += 8; news_headline = "Lewica converts PiS goodwill into neo-judge transition rules"

PiS trades transition rules for its own appointees rather than any verdict on
how they were appointed. It is the smallest agreement available, and it removes
the largest veto.

- #poland_card_finish

@ministry
title: Make the Justice Ministry produce the transition file
subtitle: Cost: 1 budget capacity. Preparation +14.
choose-if: left_in_government = 1 and budget >= 1 and justice_minister_party = "Lewica"
unavailable-subtitle: Requires the Justice portfolio and one budget point.
view-if: courts_reform_defined = 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; courts_reform_progress += 14; administrative_capacity += 2; judicial_legitimacy += 3; prosecution_oversight_capacity += 2; news_headline = "The Justice Ministry maps the KRS, neo-judge and Tribunal transition"

Every contested appointment acquires a route and a date. The repair stops being
a purge and becomes a procedure a court can uphold.

- #poland_card_finish

@palace
title: Put the constitutional transition before the President
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Presidential commitment +1; preparation +6.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The Palace delegation needs one resource.
view-if: courts_reform_defined = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
if (Q.courts_palace_president != Q.president_name) {
    Q.courts_palace_commitment = 0;
    Q.courts_palace_president = Q.president_name;
}
Q.courts_palace_commitment += 1;
Q.courts_reform_progress += 6;
Q.president_relation += 3;
Q.news_headline = "The Palace receives the constitutional transition protocol";
!}

A President whose own camp made these appointments has the narrowest ceiling in
the game on this field. The file is worth building anyway: it is what a friendly
successor signs on the first day.

- #poland_card_finish

@advance
title: Table the bill: [+ courts_reform_next_label +]
subtitle: Requires government and passage power at or above the displayed threshold; veto players may force a narrower final settlement.
view-if: courts_reform_defined = 1
choose-if: left_in_government = 1 and government_has_confidence = 1 and caretaker_government = 0 and courts_reform_power >= courts_reform_threshold
unavailable-subtitle: We either lack executive access or have not assembled enough coalition, public and presidential power.
on-arrival: reform_pressure_issue = "courts"; reform_pressure_target_stage = courts_reform_proposal_stage; reform_pressure_previous_stage = 0; reform_pressure_return_mode = "card"; reform_pressure_palace_override = 0; reform_pressure_referendum_used = 0
go-to: poland_major_reforms.resolve
